***************************** T A L Y S **************************2525 1451  190
                                                                  2525 1451  191
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   2525 1451  192
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      2525 1451  193
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    2525 1451  194
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     2525 1451  195
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  2525 1451  196
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        2525 1451  197
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    2525 1451  198
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         2525 1451  199
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      2525 1451  200
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    2525 1451  201
stored in this data file:                                         2525 1451  202
                                                                  2525 1451  203
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   2525 1451  204
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     2525 1451  205
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 2525 1451  206
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   2525 1451  207
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                2525 1451  208
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   2525 1451  209
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    2525 1451  210
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        2525 1451  211
- Recoil data                                                     2525 1451  212
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           2525 1451  213
- Total particle energy spectra                                   2525 1451  214
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      2525 1451  215
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        2525 1451  216
- Residual production cross sections                              2525 1451  217
                                                                  2525 1451  218
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            2525 1451  219
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        2525 1451  220
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   2525 1451  221
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                2525 1451  222
                                                                  2525 1451  223
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************2525 1451  224
                                                                  2525 1451  225
##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    2525 1451  226
                                                                  2525 1451  227
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       2525 1451  228
                                                                  2525 1451  229
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          2525 1451  230
                                                                  2525 1451  231
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   2525 1451  232
                                                                  2525 1451  233
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 2525 1451  234
                                                                  2525 1451  235
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     2525 1451  236
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   2525 1451  237
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             2525 1451  238
                                                                  2525 1451  239
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                2525 1451  240
                                                                  2525 1451  241
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       2525 1451  242
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  2525 1451  243
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   2525 1451  244
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  2525 1451  245
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  2525 1451  246
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 2525 1451  247
to the highest incident energy.                                   2525 1451  248
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:2525 1451  249
                                                                  2525 1451  250
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  2525 1451  251
                                                                  2525 1451  252
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    2525 1451  253
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     2525 1451  254
                                                                  2525 1451  255
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     2525 1451  256
                                                                  2525 1451  257
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    2525 1451  258
total cross section.                                              2525 1451  259
                                                                  2525 1451  260
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            2525 1451  261
                                                                  2525 1451  262
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    2525 1451  263
                                                                  2525 1451  264
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        2525 1451  265
                                                                  2525 1451  266
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  2525 1451  267
                                                                  2525 1451  268
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           2525 1451  269
                                                                  2525 1451  270
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   2525 1451  271
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        2525 1451  272
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     2525 1451  273
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         2525 1451  274
sections.                                                         2525 1451  275
                                                                  2525 1451  276
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 2525 1451  277
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 2525 1451  278
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 2525 1451  279
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 2525 1451  280
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      2525 1451  281
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       2525 1451  282
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              2525 1451  283
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  2525 1451  284
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  2525 1451  285
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  2525 1451  286
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  2525 1451  287
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  2525 1451  288
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       2525 1451  289
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        2525 1451  290
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        2525 1451  291
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        2525 1451  292
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        2525 1451  293
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        2525 1451  294
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        2525 1451  295
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        2525 1451  296
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       2525 1451  297
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        2525 1451  298
                                                                  2525 1451  299
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           2525 1451  300
                                                                  2525 1451  301
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    2525 1451  302
discrete levels.                                                  2525 1451  303
                                                                  2525 1451  304
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         2525 1451  305
                                                                  2525 1451  306
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  2525 1451  307
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   2525 1451  308
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      2525 1451  309
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  2525 1451  310
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      2525 1451  311
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         2525 1451  312
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   2525 1451  313
on an angular grid.                                               2525 1451  314
                                                                  2525 1451  315
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       2525 1451  316
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        2525 1451  317
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         2525 1451  318
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         2525 1451  319
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         2525 1451  320
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        2525 1451  321
                                                                  2525 1451  322
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     2525 1451  323
                                                                  2525 1451  324
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     2525 1451  325
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   2525 1451  326
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  2525 1451  327
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             2525 1451  328
All data are generated with TALYS.                                2525 1451  329
                                                                  2525 1451  330
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   2525 1451  331
                                                                  2525 1451  332
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      2525 1451  333
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   2525 1451  334
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   2525 1451  335
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are2525 1451  336
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   2525 1451  337
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  2525 1451  338
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              2525 1451  339
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 2525 1451  340
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  2525 1451  341
For each residual product:                                        2525 1451  342
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               2525 1451  343
- the recoil                                                      2525 1451  344
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         2525 1451  345
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     2525 1451  346
sections.                                                         2525 1451  347
                                                                  2525 1451  348
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     2525 1451  349
                                                                  2525 1451  350
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  2525 1451  351
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 2525 1451  352
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          2525 1451  353
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       2525 1451  354
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 2525 1451  355
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     2525 1451  356
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  2525 1451  357
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      2525 1451  358
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         2525 1451  359
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             2525 1451  360
                                                                  2525 1451  361
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   2525 1451  362
followed:                                                         2525 1451  363
                                                                  2525 1451  364
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         2525 1451  365
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         2525 1451  366
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         2525 1451  367
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     2525 1451  368
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2525 1451  369
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2525 1451  370
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2525 1451  371
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2525 1451  372
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2525 1451  373
                                                                  2525 1451  374
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 2525 1451  375
                                                                  2525 1451  376
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    2525 1451  377
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          2525 1451  378
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     2525 1451  379
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          2525 1451  380
                                                                  2525 1451  381
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  2525 1451  382
                                                                  2525 1451  383
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     2525 1451  384
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    2525 1451  385
as isomer.                                                        2525 1451  386
                                                                  2525 1451  387
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 2525 1451  388
                                                                  2525 1451  389
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        2525 1451  390
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    2525 1451  391
as isomer.                                                        2525 1451  392
                                                                  2525 1451  393
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          2525 1451  394
                                                                  2525 1451  395
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:2525 1451  396
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   2525 1451  397
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   2525 1451  398
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   2525 1451  399
  given                                                           2525 1451  400
                                                                  2525 1451  401
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          2525 1451  402
                                                                  2525 1451  403
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  2525 1451  404
                                                                  2525 1451  405
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 2525 1451  406
                                                                  2525 1451  407
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         2525 1451  408
                                                                  2525 1451  409
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   2525 1451  410
                                                                  2525 1451  411
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        2525 1451  412
and more details are given above in this description. In most     2525 1451  413
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        2525 1451  414
                                                                  2525 1451  415
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 2525 1451  416
                                                                  2525 1451  417
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  2525 1451  418
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     2525 1451  419
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    2525 1451  420
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   2525 1451  421
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  2525 1451  422
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                2525 1451  423
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      2525 1451  424
   same reaction channel between different energies)              2525 1451  425
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      2525 1451  426
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               2525 1451  427
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      2525 1451  428
   different reaction channels for different energies)            2525 1451  429
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        2525 1451  430
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              2525 1451  431
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  2525 1451  432
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       2525 1451  433
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     2525 1451  434
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  2525 1451  435
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     2525 1451  436
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     2525 1451  437
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     2525 1451  438
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   2525 1451  439
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   2525 1451  440
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  2525 1451  441
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   2525 1451  442
                                                                  2525 1451  443
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  2525 1451  444
                                                                  2525 1451  445
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       2525 1451  446
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  2525 1451  447
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       2525 1451  448
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   2525 1451  449
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         2525 1451  450
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  2525 1451  451
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      2525 1451  452
representation is used.                                           2525 1451  453
                                                                  2525 1451  454
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      2525 1451  455
                                                                  2525 1451  456
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  2525 1451  457
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             2525 1451  458
                                                                  2525 1451  459
